</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Model 3a: LSM, kPa</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x000a0;&#x000a0;&#x000a0;&#x000a0;</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Sex (male)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.42 (0.63-3.2)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.39</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pre-treatment LSM, kPa</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.05 (1.02-1.07)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c; 0.001</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pre-treatment age, years</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.06 (1.01-1.11)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.10</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Model 3b: LSM &#x02265; 20 kPa</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Sex (male)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.72 (0.32-1.63)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.43</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pre-treatment LSM &#x02265; 20 kPa</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.2 (0.08-0.47)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c; 0.001</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pre-treatment age, years</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.06 (1.01-1.11)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.02</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Model 3c: FIB-4 index</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Sex (male)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.41 (0.57-3.49)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.45</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pre-treatment age, years</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.06 (1.01-1.11)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.22</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pre-treatment FIB-4 index</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.13 (1.05-1.21)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c; 0.001</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Model 3d: FIB-4 index &#x02265; 3.25</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Sex (male)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.81 (0.49-2.82)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.71</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pre-treatment age, years</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.06 (1-1.11)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.034</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Pre-treatment FIB-4 index &#x02265; 3.25</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">7.79 (2.31-26.32)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x0003c; 0.001</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>HR: Hazard ratio; CI: Confidence interval; LSM: Liver stiffness measure; FIB-4: Fibrosis-4.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><p>Table <xref rid="T4" ref-type="table">4</xref> presents 1-year-EOT models regarding pre-treatment LSM as a continuous or categorical variable (Cut-off of 20 kPa), (models 4a and 4b), as well as 1-year-EOT FIB-4 index, also as a continuous or categorical variable (cut-off 3.25) (models 4c and 4d). One year-EOT-LSM either as a continuous or categorical variable (models 4a and 4b) and continuous or categorical FIB-4 index (models 4c and 4d) together with age were associated with HCC outcome. Furthermore, LSM &#x02265; 15 kPa was also performed in Cox regression analysis and showed to be significant only after 1-year-EOT (HR = 3.98, 95%CI: 1.64-9.62, <italic>P</italic> = 0.002).</p><table-wrap position="float" id="T4"><label>Table 4</label><caption><p>Cox regression models regarding post-treatment liver stiffness measure and fibrosis-4 index as continuous or categorical variables</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">
